schema: "0.4"
id: npl-editorial-26-ticket-detail
type: image
quality: high

# NoizuPromptLingo — a single work ticket with cross-references to other tickets and entities — Ticket Detail screen.
# Theme tenets: warm paper stock, serif body (Source Serif 4), single muted-claret ink accent, near-square 2px radius, warm beige hairline rules, footnote/citation sensibility.
# Palette: paper #fbf8f1, warm ink #1c1917, claret #9a2c3f, petrol #1d4e5f, ochre #b45309, beige hairline #e3d9c6.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a
    cross-referenced entry in a printed standard — calm, literate, exact, print-like.
    The body face is a SERIF; the canvas is warm off-white paper; margins are
    generous and one reading measure is protected. Cross-references and footnotes are
    idiomatic here, not clutter. NOT a cool-white SaaS ticket tracker and NOT a dark
    console. Structure comes from type hierarchy and warm hairline rules, never heavy
    borders or drop shadows.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity UI mockup of the Ticket Detail screen of NoizuPromptLingo, a
    single work ticket with cross-references to other tickets and entities. It reads
    like a cross-referenced entry in a printed standard, footnotes and citations
    idiomatic.

    OVERALL LAYOUT (two bands on a warm off-white paper canvas, separated by a warm
    beige hairline and generous margin): a dominant CENTER ticket column and a RIGHT
    references rail.

    TOP HEADER BAND: serif wordmark "NPL" at left; breadcrumb "Tickets / PRD-114" in
    serif; a monospace ticket-id chip on a warm-paper pill with near-square corners; a
    WATCH TOGGLE shown as a small typeset labelled switch ("Watching") with a petrol
    focus outline; a status label in small serif small-caps.

    CENTER TICKET COLUMN (dominant, protected reading measure): a serif H1 ticket
    title, a metadata line (author, date, priority) in warm-gray serif, then a
    LOCALIZED CONTENT RENDERER — a serif description at generous line-height that
    includes a short paragraph of non-Latin text (a French sentence with accents and
    one line of Arabic) rendered cleanly to show correct localization; one inline
    literal token in monospace; and a footnote reference at the foot of the column.
    Restrained and print-like.

    RIGHT REFERENCES RAIL (about 300px), a stack of small titled panels each headed by
    a monospace small-caps eyebrow and separated by beige hairlines:
    - TICKET LINK PANEL: two "blocks" / "relates to" rows, each a serif ticket title
      with a monospace id and a small relation label.
    - POLYMORPHIC LINK PANEL: two rows linking non-ticket entities (a wiki page, an
      artifact) with small type glyphs; one row is an ORPHANED-LINK PLACEHOLDER shown
      muted and italic ("linked item no longer exists") with a faint dashed beige rule
      — gracefully degraded, not an error.
    - LINKED USER STORIES LIST: three rolled-up story rows (monospace "US-014" tags +
      short serif titles), marked as under this PRD.

    Links and relation labels take deep petrol teal; the active/watched affordances
    take muted claret; nothing shouts.

    PALETTE & TYPE: warm off-white paper, warm near-black serif ink, one muted claret
    accent, deep petrol teal for links and cross-references, warm-gray meta,
    burnt-ochre used sparingly. Warm beige hairlines, never cool gray. Serif (Source
    Serif 4) for all prose; monospace only for ticket/story ids and literal tokens. No
    geometric sans.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: near-square 2px corners, flat and tonal, separation by hairline
    and margin rather than shadow; a faint paper grain on the canvas.

    MOOD: considered, exact, literate — a cross-referenced spec entry you cite, warm
    and durable as printed paper.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Shows the ticket body with correctly-rendered non-Latin content, a ticket link panel, a polymorphic link panel with an orphaned-link placeholder, a linked user stories list, and a watch toggle"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Warm paper canvas, serif body/headings, single muted-claret accent, petrol cross-reference links, warm beige hairlines, near-square 2px radius — not a generic SaaS tracker"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Clear visual hierarchy, protected reading measure, plausible ticket-detail layout"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"

tags: [npl-editorial, NoizuPromptLingo, screen-mockup]
